WEBVTT

00:00:12.090 --> 00:00:13.550
Allow me to introduce you.

00:00:15.090 --> 00:00:17.350
This is my wife.

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:20.140
What's the meaning of this, Edward?!

00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:24.060
I have already been formally
wed to this lady, Elizabeth.

00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:27.690
I therefore cannot marry Lady Bona.

00:00:29.110 --> 00:00:34.400
My king, do you realize
what you are saying?

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:38.030
A sovereign's marriage
is not a personal matter.

00:00:38.030 --> 00:00:39.990
I understand that,

00:00:39.990 --> 00:00:42.250
but I can't help having met her!

00:00:42.250 --> 00:00:45.170
I cannot undo my compact
with the King of France!

00:00:45.170 --> 00:00:47.670
Nor I my compact with God!

00:00:47.670 --> 00:00:51.800
How could you put base lusts
before the good of England?

00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:54.220
Make your choice: that woman, or me!

00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:56.470
I choose love!

00:00:56.470 --> 00:00:59.550
Oh, I can't keep myself from smiling.

00:00:59.550 --> 00:01:04.060
Now I'm queen in fact as well as name.

00:01:09.650 --> 00:01:11.690
York of the white rose.

00:01:11.690 --> 00:01:14.320
Lancaster of the red rose.

00:01:14.320 --> 00:01:20.740
These royal houses with roses
for their crests battled for the throne.

00:01:20.740 --> 00:01:25.410
People call their strife
the "Wars of the Roses."

00:03:04.930 --> 00:03:08.640
God save Her Majesty, Queen Elizabeth!

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:15.520
Have you heard?

00:03:15.520 --> 00:03:19.900
Queen Elizabeth's younger sister
married the Duke of Buckingham.

00:03:19.900 --> 00:03:24.990
But the queen's family is too
lowly to marry into a dukedom.

00:03:24.990 --> 00:03:29.540
The leading nobles of the realm
are bowing and scraping to us.

00:03:29.540 --> 00:03:34.040
Not even the Kingmaker can ignore me now.

00:03:34.040 --> 00:03:35.630
Lord Warwick.

00:03:38.380 --> 00:03:41.220
Excuse me. Who might you be?

00:03:43.090 --> 00:03:44.970
You must be joking.

00:03:44.970 --> 00:03:48.520
Surely you haven't forgotten
your queen's younger brother?

00:03:48.520 --> 00:03:50.230
I beg your pardon.

00:03:50.230 --> 00:03:56.060
Her Majesty's whim brings more
parvenus to court almost daily of late.

00:03:57.610 --> 00:03:59.780
By the way, my lord,

00:03:59.780 --> 00:04:03.320
have you given our reply
to the King of France yet?

00:04:04.490 --> 00:04:06.160
I can't believe it.

00:04:06.160 --> 00:04:08.080
He's the king of a whole country.

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:10.870
He could've at least
consulted us or his council.

00:04:10.870 --> 00:04:13.920
Does my marriage displease you?

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:16.170
I agree with Warwick.

00:04:16.170 --> 00:04:20.960
Then I suppose you're
still my only ally, Richard.

00:04:20.960 --> 00:04:22.470
Even now.

00:04:22.470 --> 00:04:26.800
Richard, don't tell me
you knew about this!

00:04:26.800 --> 00:04:28.890
I'm not on anyone's side.

00:04:31.350 --> 00:04:32.890
It's going to be war.

00:04:33.850 --> 00:04:36.600
There will be war with France,
mark my words.

00:04:36.600 --> 00:04:39.020
Why do you think so?

00:04:39.020 --> 00:04:41.780
Because your brother acted the fool.

00:04:41.780 --> 00:04:43.740
Watch your tongue, brat.

00:04:43.740 --> 00:04:44.990
I'm no brat.

00:04:44.990 --> 00:04:46.910
I'm the Duke of Buckingham.

00:04:46.910 --> 00:04:52.080
The one your brother saddled with
some provincial dame for a wife.

00:04:52.080 --> 00:04:53.960
You're an amusing fellow.

00:04:55.290 --> 00:04:58.630
It seems you speak my language, Richard.

00:05:00.920 --> 00:05:03.760
I prefer women of lofty status.

00:05:06.010 --> 00:05:06.970
Hey.

00:05:07.840 --> 00:05:08.970
Ow!

00:05:08.970 --> 00:05:11.680
I'm no woman, Duke.

00:05:12.680 --> 00:05:16.100
I hear the French king, Louis,
is a cautious man.

00:05:16.100 --> 00:05:18.810
I doubt he'd be so quick to raise an army.

00:05:24.400 --> 00:05:28.160
King Edward was married already, you say?

00:05:28.160 --> 00:05:32.080
Is this the amity that England
seeks with France?

00:05:32.080 --> 00:05:33.830
Warwick,

00:05:33.830 --> 00:05:39.920
have you not sacrificed much
to set a crown upon his head?

00:05:39.920 --> 00:05:42.380
Is this your reward?

00:05:42.380 --> 00:05:46.220
Will you still call him your king?

00:05:49.720 --> 00:05:53.260
If we get another war to turn
the world upside down,

00:05:53.260 --> 00:05:56.690
then even I might end up king.

00:05:56.690 --> 00:06:00.190
If you weren't a child,
I'd lop off your head for treason.

00:06:00.190 --> 00:06:02.940
Haven't you ever considered it, Richard?!

00:06:02.940 --> 00:06:05.070
You could be king yourself!

00:06:06.400 --> 00:06:08.820
Me, king?

00:06:08.820 --> 00:06:09.910
That's right.

00:06:09.910 --> 00:06:14.620
Needless to say, there are a lot of
people between us and the crown.

00:06:14.620 --> 00:06:17.460
It's like a lightless forest of briars.

00:06:17.460 --> 00:06:23.550
But if war breaks out, we could blaze
a trail through it with our axes!

00:06:23.550 --> 00:06:26.050
Can your scrawny arms lift an axe?

00:06:26.050 --> 00:06:30.970
Not now, but if you feel inclined
to carry one in my place...

00:06:32.800 --> 00:06:36.520
...then becoming your very own
kingmaker sounds like fun.

00:06:48.950 --> 00:06:51.870
Me, become king?

00:06:51.870 --> 00:06:55.200
With this shameful body of mine?

00:06:55.200 --> 00:06:58.000
Don't dream of the impossible.

00:06:58.000 --> 00:07:01.120
There's no kingdom for me.

00:07:01.120 --> 00:07:05.090
But who's worthy to be king if I'm not?

00:07:05.090 --> 00:07:07.590
Father is no longer with us.

00:07:07.590 --> 00:07:10.090
Is Edward worthy of the crown?

00:07:10.090 --> 00:07:13.550
Is Henry, or his son?

00:07:13.550 --> 00:07:14.850
Never.

00:07:18.930 --> 00:07:23.940
Preserve my name, Richard.
It's the name of a king.

00:07:27.030 --> 00:07:28.990
The name... of a king.

00:07:32.860 --> 00:07:36.030
Your Majesty, Henry's
transport is complete.

00:07:36.030 --> 00:07:37.870
How pitiful.

00:07:37.870 --> 00:07:42.960
A former king, captured by
peasants, of all people?

00:07:42.960 --> 00:07:44.960
Does Richard know of this?

00:07:44.960 --> 00:07:50.010
The Duke of Gloucester hasn't
found out yet, but when he does...

00:07:50.010 --> 00:07:53.130
I suppose I'd better keep him
out of London for a while.

00:07:53.130 --> 00:07:54.680
As a matter of fact,

00:07:54.680 --> 00:07:59.140
the Earl of Warwick made
a request on that subject.

00:07:59.140 --> 00:08:01.940
I gave orders to admit no one.

00:08:01.940 --> 00:08:04.480
That servant is out of a job.

00:08:04.480 --> 00:08:10.610
No one in this realm can
defy my command, Richard.

00:08:10.610 --> 00:08:13.150
No one but the king.

00:08:13.150 --> 00:08:17.660
I only take orders from the true king.

00:08:17.660 --> 00:08:19.540
Aren't you the same?

00:08:19.540 --> 00:08:21.500
Don't touch my father.

00:08:21.500 --> 00:08:24.000
What brings you here?

00:08:24.000 --> 00:08:26.080
I've come to collect you.

00:08:37.010 --> 00:08:40.890
Warwick is riding with Richard?
What is he scheming?

00:08:43.890 --> 00:08:46.270
Welcome to Middleham Castle.

00:08:46.270 --> 00:08:49.570
Welcome home, Father.

00:08:49.570 --> 00:08:53.280
You'll be living with us
here for a short while.

00:08:53.280 --> 00:08:56.700
Anne, Isabelle, be on your best behavior.

00:09:09.630 --> 00:09:12.630
I've grown much stronger since then.

00:09:12.630 --> 00:09:15.470
I've learned to fight.

00:09:15.470 --> 00:09:18.640
I've matured as a man.

00:09:18.640 --> 00:09:22.100
And yet, my body always remains imperfect.

00:09:27.600 --> 00:09:29.230
I'm deluding myself.

00:09:31.820 --> 00:09:34.150
It's no delusion, Richard.

00:09:34.150 --> 00:09:37.110
You're in love with Henry.

00:09:37.110 --> 00:09:38.410
Stop.

00:09:39.200 --> 00:09:41.370
You really long to--

00:09:41.370 --> 00:09:43.580
Stop! I'm not a woman!

00:09:43.580 --> 00:09:46.620
Women style their long hair, wear dresses,

00:09:46.620 --> 00:09:49.170
and wait at home for
the men who defend them!

00:09:49.170 --> 00:09:50.460
So, I'm not a woman!

00:09:50.460 --> 00:09:53.710
Anne! You've got to talk to him!

00:09:53.710 --> 00:09:59.010
But I've sent him so many letters,
and he's never answered any of them.

00:10:00.050 --> 00:10:01.680
A boar?

00:10:01.680 --> 00:10:04.020
Hey. Stop that, Whitey.

00:10:04.020 --> 00:10:07.730
I'm sorry. It's normally better behaved.

00:10:09.400 --> 00:10:12.360
Is this the boar from back then?

00:10:12.360 --> 00:10:16.900
I always thought it ended up being
served at that night's dinner.

00:10:19.950 --> 00:10:21.320
Anne!

00:10:24.240 --> 00:10:28.040
I-I'll be your training partner!

00:10:28.040 --> 00:10:29.580
I'm a good rider!

00:10:29.580 --> 00:10:34.130
I-I can outride any
gentleman in the castle.

00:10:37.550 --> 00:10:39.340
Oh, my, Anne.

00:10:39.340 --> 00:10:41.970
The hem of your dress is torn!

00:10:41.970 --> 00:10:44.810
Could that boar be to blame?

00:10:44.810 --> 00:10:48.640
Surely, damaging a lady's
dress requires an apology?

00:10:51.150 --> 00:10:52.980
You've forced my hand.

00:10:52.980 --> 00:10:55.780
But in exchange, I won't go easy on you,

00:10:55.780 --> 00:10:56.780
Anne.

00:11:00.410 --> 00:11:03.160
Duke Richard! Over here!

00:11:10.460 --> 00:11:11.960
I'll admit it.

00:11:11.960 --> 00:11:15.300
Your horsemanship is impressive.

00:11:15.300 --> 00:11:16.760
Truly?

00:11:16.760 --> 00:11:17.960
I'm so glad.

00:11:17.960 --> 00:11:22.890
I've always been jealous of boys,
ever since I was little.

00:11:22.890 --> 00:11:26.680
To be honest, I would have
much rather ridden off to battle

00:11:26.680 --> 00:11:29.390
than sat around in dresses
doing embroidery.

00:11:29.390 --> 00:11:33.860
But when my father hears me say so,
he scolds me for my ignorance

00:11:33.860 --> 00:11:35.900
of the horrors of war.

00:11:35.900 --> 00:11:37.070
No.

00:11:37.070 --> 00:11:40.860
If you'd been a man, I'm sure you
would have made a fine knight.

00:11:43.110 --> 00:11:44.120
Thank you.

00:11:49.660 --> 00:11:51.500
Oh, look, Duke Richard!

00:11:51.500 --> 00:11:53.210
So many acorns!

00:11:53.210 --> 00:11:58.210
Let's scoop some up to bring home.
I'm sure that Whitey will love them.

00:11:59.840 --> 00:12:03.220
Anne is different from other women.

00:12:04.970 --> 00:12:10.390
It's strange. Being with her
puts my mind at ease.

00:12:10.390 --> 00:12:14.270
She doesn't disturb
my thoughts like he does.

00:12:15.770 --> 00:12:20.780
In fact, when we're like this,
I feel like I could forget everything.

00:12:20.780 --> 00:12:23.240
Oh, no! The acorns.

00:12:23.240 --> 00:12:25.910
Should we wrap them in a cloak to carry?

00:12:25.910 --> 00:12:29.370
We should make another trip.
We can bring Whitey.

00:12:32.580 --> 00:12:35.290
I just have to avoid getting too close,

00:12:35.290 --> 00:12:38.420
so that I won't fear losing you.

00:12:38.420 --> 00:12:42.760
If I don't grab your hand,
I won't have to let go.

00:12:47.760 --> 00:12:52.680
How could a sacred king take
a woman like her for his wife?

00:12:52.680 --> 00:12:55.690
Edward shows Richard too much favor.

00:12:55.690 --> 00:12:59.320
I was his favorite before
his marriage, but now...

00:12:59.320 --> 00:13:03.990
Honestly, Duke George!
You've spoken of nothing but King Edward!

00:13:03.990 --> 00:13:06.450
I haven't had a chance
to see you in so long.

00:13:06.450 --> 00:13:08.490
I'm sorry, Isabelle.

00:13:08.490 --> 00:13:14.910
Still, is King Edward really
suited for a sacred throne?

00:13:16.960 --> 00:13:23.470
You seem like you would make
a far better king to me.

00:13:23.470 --> 00:13:24.760
Isabelle.

00:13:30.970 --> 00:13:33.520
Oh, Duke George. You mustn't.

00:13:36.100 --> 00:13:38.770
Would you care for another cup?

00:13:40.320 --> 00:13:43.530
Warwick? What brings you--

00:13:43.530 --> 00:13:48.030
I cannot countenance congress
before marriage, My Lord Duke.

00:13:48.030 --> 00:13:49.950
O-Oh, well, this isn't--

00:13:49.950 --> 00:13:52.620
Did you not say so yourself?

00:13:52.620 --> 00:13:56.920
Such a woman should not
be the wife of a king.

00:13:56.920 --> 00:14:00.090
I must ask you to restrain yourself.

00:14:00.090 --> 00:14:04.170
This is the precious body
of a future queen.

00:14:04.170 --> 00:14:06.550
A queen?

00:14:06.550 --> 00:14:09.300
Isabelle? Of what country?

00:14:12.890 --> 00:14:15.180
Of yours,

00:14:15.180 --> 00:14:16.520
Your Majesty.

00:14:29.530 --> 00:14:31.280
Another cold day.

00:14:34.450 --> 00:14:36.830
Shh! Keep quiet!

00:14:38.830 --> 00:14:42.960
U-Um... I was planning to wait
until you finished working.

00:14:42.960 --> 00:14:47.220
You'll take ill. It's so cold
that the rivers have frozen.

00:14:47.220 --> 00:14:49.300
Y-Yes, they have!

00:14:49.300 --> 00:14:52.050
That's why I hoped you would
go skating with me!

00:14:53.890 --> 00:14:58.270
Are you really sure about this?
You were in the middle of business.

00:14:58.270 --> 00:15:01.900
I'd just started feeling sluggish.

00:15:01.900 --> 00:15:05.530
I'm more concerned about your footing.

00:15:05.530 --> 00:15:07.530
I-I'll be fine!

00:15:07.530 --> 00:15:09.950
I've skated lots of times before.

00:15:12.240 --> 00:15:16.290
Let's race each other to that tree!

00:15:16.290 --> 00:15:17.410
I don't mind.

00:15:17.410 --> 00:15:18.910
You won't beat me!

00:15:23.170 --> 00:15:28.050
The time I spend with Anne does more
than anything else to stabilize me.

00:15:28.050 --> 00:15:31.220
Anne allows me to be myself.

00:15:32.800 --> 00:15:35.220
Duke Richard! Victory is mi--

00:15:38.930 --> 00:15:41.520
I've never felt this way...

00:15:42.940 --> 00:15:46.190
...about another person before.

00:15:49.070 --> 00:15:51.280
Anne, your foot.

00:15:51.280 --> 00:15:53.820
Excuse me. It was untied.

00:15:53.820 --> 00:15:56.240
O-Oh, no.

00:15:56.240 --> 00:15:57.950
Please don't mention it.

00:16:04.130 --> 00:16:05.790
What a blunder.

00:16:05.790 --> 00:16:08.760
You couldn't help it
in this freezing weather.

00:16:08.760 --> 00:16:14.220
What a shame. I was hoping
to make a snowman next.

00:16:14.220 --> 00:16:15.800
Together.

00:16:17.010 --> 00:16:20.560
Is making a snowman too childish?

00:16:20.560 --> 00:16:25.270
No, but I'm not confident
I could do it well.

00:16:25.270 --> 00:16:28.610
I've only made one once,
when I was little.

00:16:28.610 --> 00:16:32.990
I was staring outside on my own,
so my attendant taught me how.

00:16:36.950 --> 00:16:41.540
Was that attendant Mr. Catesby,
by any chance?

00:16:41.540 --> 00:16:44.290
Yes, it was. How did you know?

00:16:44.290 --> 00:16:46.250
I remember him.

00:16:46.250 --> 00:16:51.090
I mean, he was always by your side.

00:16:52.670 --> 00:16:58.680
That was the first time Duke Richard
ever told me about his childhood.

00:16:58.680 --> 00:17:00.020
I'm so happy.

00:17:03.230 --> 00:17:07.730
Do you know what kind
of presents women like?

00:17:07.730 --> 00:17:10.150
How should I know?

00:17:10.150 --> 00:17:12.240
You're a woman, technically.

00:17:12.240 --> 00:17:15.950
I told you, I'm you.

00:17:15.950 --> 00:17:20.240
Half of you is a woman,
so you should know too.

00:17:20.240 --> 00:17:24.330
I wouldn't be happy to get
dresses or hair ornaments.

00:17:24.330 --> 00:17:25.960
I'm not a woman.

00:17:25.960 --> 00:17:28.630
See? You do know.

00:17:28.630 --> 00:17:32.460
You haven't been yourself these days.

00:17:32.460 --> 00:17:34.800
I mean, you're reading romances.

00:17:38.850 --> 00:17:43.680
Loving a woman doesn't
make you a man, you know.

00:17:43.680 --> 00:17:46.190
I've always been a man!

00:17:46.190 --> 00:17:49.310
Oh, I was talking about this book.

00:17:49.310 --> 00:17:52.570
I'm just wishing her well.
Don't get the wrong idea.

00:17:52.570 --> 00:17:54.190
Exactly!

00:17:54.190 --> 00:17:57.660
You'd better forget about happy endings

00:17:57.660 --> 00:18:00.530
unless you can believe to the bitter end.

00:18:03.540 --> 00:18:05.960
I'm not hoping for one.

00:18:05.960 --> 00:18:11.170
It's... It's just that Anne
isn't like other women.

00:18:12.590 --> 00:18:14.090
Where is George?

00:18:14.090 --> 00:18:18.260
With His Majesty,
asking leave to marry me.

00:18:18.260 --> 00:18:24.350
Asking leave? The king himself
already proved that unnecessary.

00:18:24.350 --> 00:18:28.650
I can't rely on George to
dethrone the king as he is.

00:18:28.650 --> 00:18:31.730
I'll need other allies.

00:18:34.940 --> 00:18:37.450
Anne, you look well.

00:18:37.450 --> 00:18:39.660
Yes, I feel much better.

00:18:39.660 --> 00:18:42.200
Thanks to Richard's visit, I suppose.

00:18:43.870 --> 00:18:45.700
Keep it up.

00:18:45.700 --> 00:18:50.210
Continue seducing Richard
until he's infatuated with you.

00:18:50.210 --> 00:18:52.630
"S-Seducing"?

00:18:52.630 --> 00:18:55.960
What an awful way to put it, Father!

00:18:55.960 --> 00:18:58.220
He's still young.

00:18:58.220 --> 00:19:00.760
He can't resist the lure
of a woman's body.

00:19:00.760 --> 00:19:04.970
Stop it. It's not like that between us.

00:19:04.970 --> 00:19:06.980
Listen, Anne.

00:19:06.980 --> 00:19:09.440
I'm going to marry you to Richard.

00:19:11.690 --> 00:19:15.570
You must understand the
Nevilles' current circumstances.

00:19:15.570 --> 00:19:19.200
We need Richard's support.

00:19:20.030 --> 00:19:22.660
You mean you plan to use Duke Richard?

00:19:22.660 --> 00:19:24.120
Naturally.

00:19:24.120 --> 00:19:25.910
It's an aristocratic marriage.

00:19:26.830 --> 00:19:31.210
But Duke Richard is so
kind and pure of heart.

00:19:33.420 --> 00:19:34.880
No!

00:19:34.880 --> 00:19:36.130
Anne.

00:19:36.130 --> 00:19:38.420
I refuse!

00:19:38.420 --> 00:19:42.010
I've never defied you before, Father,

00:19:42.010 --> 00:19:43.930
but this is too far!

00:19:43.930 --> 00:19:48.350
I'll arrange the match,
even if it isn't to your liking.

00:19:48.350 --> 00:19:50.810
Even if you don't love Richard.

00:19:53.310 --> 00:19:58.400
You need only continue to captivate
his heart as you have been.

00:19:58.400 --> 00:20:00.740
I won't do it!

00:20:00.740 --> 00:20:04.240
I-I'll never marry like that!

00:20:04.240 --> 00:20:06.740
I refuse to marry Duke Richard!

00:20:15.960 --> 00:20:17.840
Because I...

00:20:17.840 --> 00:20:19.630
I really do...

00:20:19.630 --> 00:20:23.050
I really do care for him.

00:20:29.560 --> 00:20:32.230
What an idiotic blunder.

00:20:32.230 --> 00:20:35.230
I know how suspicious Richard is.

00:20:35.230 --> 00:20:39.070
I'll never be able to
win him over after this.

00:20:39.070 --> 00:20:41.900
History has gone astray,
and I must set it right.

00:20:41.900 --> 00:20:46.990
He was the true king, not his son!

00:20:46.990 --> 00:20:51.200
I am the Kingmaker, and I'll decide
who is fit to wear the crown.

00:20:52.660 --> 00:20:57.750
Richard is with the Earl of Warwick?
I hope he'll be all right.

00:20:57.750 --> 00:21:00.340
There's nothing to worry about.

00:21:00.340 --> 00:21:02.840
This is a message to Warwick.

00:21:02.840 --> 00:21:04.880
A message?

00:21:04.880 --> 00:21:09.760
Yes. I'm telling him that I trust him.

00:21:09.760 --> 00:21:13.560
You should just focus on
the child you're carrying.

00:21:13.560 --> 00:21:15.230
I suppose.

00:21:15.230 --> 00:21:19.070
I don't love you. Not one bit.

00:21:19.070 --> 00:21:23.530
Once Edward is dead and my child is king,

00:21:23.530 --> 00:21:29.410
the Woodvilles will hold all power,
and my revenge will be complete.

00:21:29.410 --> 00:21:34.080
Come out nice and healthy now,
my little trump card.

00:21:35.830 --> 00:21:38.920
Aren't you glad, Richard?

00:21:38.920 --> 00:21:41.710
This had to happen sooner or later.

00:21:41.710 --> 00:21:44.220
You must have known that.

00:21:44.220 --> 00:21:48.760
No one will love you
but blood and the dead.

00:21:53.020 --> 00:21:55.020
That's right, Richard.

00:21:55.020 --> 00:21:58.900
Fall into the warm depths of darkness.
